## Plan

#3568: stall-recovery `bug-body` is unparseable by `/larch:issue --input-file`

## Summary

`/implement` Step 18a first-detection filing pipes the heading-less `bug-body` output straight into `/larch:issue --input-file`. The generic batch parser (`skills/issue/scripts/parse-input.sh`) requires a `### <title>` item heading, so it returns `ITEMS_TOTAL=0` and files nothing — silently.

The repo already ships the fix as a tested subcommand: `stall-recovery-report.sh issue-input-file` synthesizes the `### [Bug] /implement stall: <class> at <step>` heading from the classification env plus the `bug-body` output. It is simply never called from `stall-recovery.md` step 4. This plan wires it in, normalizes batch-mode `/issue` stdout into `stall-recovery-issue.env`, tightens step-token sanitization for public issue titles, and pins all three surfaces so the bug cannot silently re-break.

